exactly, it is unfortunate but eventually the burden will fall to the humans who handcraft to verify their work is human made. We need to push development so that this becomes an easy task. 

Right now some of the model providers (i know for sure anthropic does) watermark their output, we need to figure out collectively how to improve these types of ways to distinguish human made content in all domains, otherwise we risk an unnecessary future where next generations simply are not interested in becoming artists because of lack of incentives.
